     "text": "Not compiled or run on the device yet. The kernel is meant to stream `x` once through SBUF, double each tile on VectorE, and write each tile once to a new output.\n\n- **Split across cores:** under LNC=2 the two physical cores each take one contiguous half of `x`.\n- **Tile layout:** each half is viewed as `(T, 128, F)` tiles. Each partition reads one contiguous `F`-element piece per tile.\n- **Tile size `F`:** `run()` sets it from the shape alone. For per-core, per-partition length `C = n/256`, the target is `min(4096, max(1024, C//8))`. `F` is the largest divisor of `C` not above that target.\n- **Why that size:** it gives at least 4\u20138 tiles per core so loads, compute and stores overlap. Each partition chunk stays at 2 KB or more. `F` always divides the work, so there are no tails for any configured `n`.\n- **Shape limit:** `run()` raises an error if `n` is not a multiple of 256. The task's `n` values are always multiples of 1,048,576, so this never triggers for them.\n- **Exactness:** the multiply by 2.0 runs in fp32 inside the engine and is cast back to fp16. Doubling is exact, so this matches `x * 2`.\n\n```python title=\"impl_nki.py\"\nimport torch\nimport nki\nimport nki.language as nl\nimport nki.isa as nisa\n\nP = 128\n\n_LAST_CONFIG = {}\n\n\n@nki.jit\ndef mul2_kernel(x, F):\n    # x: (n,) in HBM; n == num_programs * T * 128 * F (guaranteed by run()).\n    n = x.shape[0]\n    out = nl.ndarray((n,), dtype=x.dtype, buffer=nl.shared_hbm)\n    n_prog = nl.num_programs()\n    pid = nl.program_id(0)\n    chunk = P * F\n    NT = n // chunk\n    T = NT // n_prog\n    x3 = x.reshape((NT, P, F))\n    o3 = out.reshape((NT, P, F))\n    for i in range(T):\n        ti = pid * T + i\n        t = nl.ndarray((P, F), dtype=x.dtype, buffer=nl.sbuf)\n        nisa.dma_copy(dst=t, src=x3[ti])\n        nisa.tensor_scalar(dst=t, data=t, op0=nl.multiply, operand0=2.0,\n                           engine=nisa.engine.vector)\n        nisa.dma_copy(dst=o3[ti], src=t)\n    return out\n\n\ndef _choose_tile(n):\n    # per-program, per-partition column count (2 programs under LNC=2)\n    if n % (2 * P) != 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"mul2: n must be a multiple of 256 for this implementation\")\n    C = n // (2 * P)\n    f_target = min(4096, max(1024, C // 8))\n    if f_target > C:\n        f_target = C\n    F = f_target\n    while F > 1 and C % F != 0:\n        F -= 1\n    return F, C\n\n\ndef run(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    global _LAST_CONFIG\n    n = x.numel()\n    F, C = _choose_tile(n)\n    tiles_per_prog = C // F\n    _LAST_CONFIG = {\n        \"programs\": 2,\n        \"partitions\": P,\n        \"tile_free\": F,\n        \"tiles_per_program\": tiles_per_prog,\n        \"engine\": \"vector\",\n        \"op\": \"tensor_scalar_multiply_2\",\n    }\n    return mul2_kernel(x, F)\n\n\ndef get_last_config() -> dict:\n    return dict(_LAST_CONFIG)\n```",
